  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-EC_INTPA" secondary-reporter="0" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Commission - Directorate-General for International Partnerships</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evaluation of the recent and current engagement of the EU in supporting Public Financial Management reforms in Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;global objective&lt;/strong&gt; of this evaluation is twofold:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;to provide the relevant services of the European Union, the interested stakeholders and the wider public with an overall independent assessment of the performance of the Public Financial Management Reform programmes&lt;em&gt;,&lt;/em&gt; paying particular attention to its different levels of results measured against its expected objectives and to the reasons underpinning such results; and&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;to identify key lessons learned, conclusions and related recommendations in order to &lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;inform decision makers&lt;/span&gt; on how to improve future interventions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;specific objective 1&lt;/strong&gt; includes the &lt;em&gt;ex-post&lt;/em&gt; evaluation of EU support to Public Financial Management Reform Programme &#xbf; Stage III (2) (2019-2021) and assessing whether the programme&#xbf;s objectives have been met and ascertain how it contributed to better aggregate fiscal discipline, improved strategic allocation of resources and operational efficiency of allocation of resources, using qualitative and quantitative examples. On the basis of its findings, specific objective 1 includes the provision of key recommendations for future support.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;specific objective 2 &lt;/strong&gt;includes a&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;mid-term evaluation of the EU-Cambodia Partnership for Public Financial Management Reform (Stage IV) including year 1 (2022),2 (2023) and 3 (until mid-2024) of the programme and assessing whether the programme&#xbf;s objectives have been met and ascertain how it contributed to better aggregate fiscal discipline, improved strategic allocation of resources and operational efficiency of allocation of resources, using qualitative and quantitative examples. On the basis of its findings, specific objective 2 includes the provision of key recommendations for future support.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
